  "insight": {
    "title": "Why AB is a stronger medial carrier",
    "body": "AB is simultaneously the radius of both circle Gestalten and a side of the derived triangle. AC and BC inherit that same radius identity through the shared intersection C. The equilateral triangle is therefore a stabilization of one radius genealogy across three triangle sides, not just a static equality label."
  }
